// MYSTERY-O-MATIC — starter template (timed testimony mysteries)
//
// Unlike Murdle's snapshot, these run on a CLOCK: testimony is
// "X was in R from t1 to t2", and the deduction is about windows.
//   1. set the clock and the time of death from the puzzle
//   2. build the map: rooms + door(to) connections
//   3. transcribe each testimony as a leap in + a leap back to
//      unknown when it ends (persistence is a claim — when someone's
//      account runs out, return them; the amber lint watches for it)
//   4. gate each testimony with a check over its window
// Solved = checks green, could() narrowed, sole() names one.
theme paper
clock 4:00 minute(0.5)
time time_of_death 4:45

room unknown size(8 2.5 5) at(-9 0 -9) color(black)
room room_one color(seagreen)
room room_two west-of(room_one) door(to room_one) color(coral)
room room_three west-of(room_two) door(to room_two) color(tan)

//victim: found in ___ at ___
person body at(unknown 3.5 1.5) color(grey)
turn body to(90 0 0) over(0)

set suspects
person suspect_one at(unknown -3 -1) color(firebrick)
person suspect_two at(unknown -2 -1) color(steelblue)
person suspect_three at(unknown -1 -1) color(seagreen)
end

// ---- TESTIMONY -------------------------------------------------------
// the pattern, worked once (replace with your puzzle's accounts):
// "suspect_one says: I was in room_one from 4:10 to 4:30"
walk suspect_one to(room_one) over(0) start(4:10)
walk suspect_one to(unknown -3 -1) over(0) start(4:30)
check always in(suspect_one room_one) during(4:10 4:30)
// a leap (over(0)) places without a route — honest about what you
// don't know; chain walks through door markers when a route is known

// ---- QUESTIONS — watch these narrow as testimony lands ---------------
// who CANNOT be cleared for the scene of the crime?
?- could(suspects, X, room_one, time_of_death)
// the verdict: exactly one candidate left
?- sole(suspects, X, room_one, time_of_death)
// where was everyone at the fatal moment?
?- set_member(suspects, X), where(X, time_of_death, R)
